<div id="p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:173%;">Appendix</span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix S1 </span>Theoretical Explanation of Efficiency Gains</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">I now further investigate why the SRI framework can yield efficiency gains compared to existing methods in general. To compare Surrogate Representation Inference (SRI) with the existing bias-correction approach, I first define each semiparametric model and the corresponding tangent space. Let <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{SRI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{SRI}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a semiparametric model of Surrogate Representation Inference (SRI) and <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math> be that of the existing bias-correction methodology. Then, the observed data for each semiparametric model, denoted as <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\text{SRI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\text{SRI}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\text{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\text{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, are written as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex23.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Surrogate Representation Inference:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O_{\text{SRI}}=\{T_{i},\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i},G_{S_{i}}(\tilde{L}_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O_{\text{SRI}}=\{T_{i},\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i},G_{S_{i}}(\tilde{L}_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex24.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Existing Methods:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O_{\text{PPI}}=\{T_{i},\bm{h}(\mathbf{Y}_{i}),\mathbf{Z}_{i},S_{i},G_{S_{i}}(\tilde{L}_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O_{\text{PPI}}=\{T_{i},\bm{h}(\mathbf{Y}_{i}),\mathbf{Z}_{i},S_{i},G_{S_{i}}(\tilde{L}_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the predictor of interest, <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of control variables, <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the human annotation, <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator variable for whether the human annotation <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is observed, <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{S_{i}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{S_{i}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the coarsening operator that outputs the input when <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and outputs the empty set when <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{h}(\bm{Y}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{h}(\bm{Y}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is the machine learning-based proxy. Importantly, texts <math id="A1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the independence <math id="A1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{i}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ T_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{i}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ T_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, but this is not necessarily true for <math id="A1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{h}(\bm{Y}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{h}(\bm{Y}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. As a result, without any constraints on machine learning predictions, <math id="A1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{SRI}}\subseteq\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>SRI</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>PPI</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{SRI}}\subseteq\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math>
since any factorization under <math id="A1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{SRI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>SRI</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{SRI}}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to <math id="A1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>PPI</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As a result, the tangent space of Surrogate Representation Inference, denoted
as <math id="A1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{SRI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>SRI</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{SRI}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is a linear subspace of that of the existing method <math id="A1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>PPI</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In semiparametric statistics, the model’s efficiency is often evaluated in terms of the <em id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">semiparametric efficiency bound</em>, which is the analogue of the Cramér-Rao lower bound for the semiparametric problem and no semiparametric estimators can have an asymptotic variance smaller than this bound (e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bickel et al. 1993</a>; <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Newey 1990</a>; <a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaart 1998</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tsiatis 2006</a></cite>). To see the efficiency gains, I compare the efficiency bounds for the two different methods. Mathematically, they are given by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex25.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Surrogate Representation Inference:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex26.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Existing Methods:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{i}=\{T_{i},\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{i}=\{T_{i},\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of variables required to consider the score, <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(O_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(O_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is the score function, and <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pi(\cdot\mid\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi(\cdot\mid\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the projection operator (note that I can remove <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> when considering the score since it is a deterministic function of <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>). As <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}}\subseteq\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}}\subseteq\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})}_{\text{Efficient Score for SRI}}=\underbrace{S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})}_{\text{Efficient Score for PPI}}+\underbrace{\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})}_{:=\Delta\ (\text{residual term)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>Efficient Score for SRI</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>Efficient Score for PPI</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.410em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>residual term)</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})}_{\text{Efficient Score for SRI}}=\underbrace{S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})}_{\text{Efficient Score for PPI}}+\underbrace{\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})}_{:=\Delta\ (\text{residual term)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where the residual term <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is orthogonal to the efficient score for PPI. As a result, since <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\in\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\in\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the efficient score belongs to the orthogonal complement of the tangent space,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})+\Delta\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})+\Delta\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})+\Delta\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})+\Delta\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]+\mathbb{E}[\Delta\Delta^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]+\mathbb{E}[\Delta\Delta^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\succeq\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\succeq\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where the third equality is by the orthogonality of the residual term to the efficient score that lies in the orthocomplement of the tangent space. Therefore, as most of the existing literature on the bias-correction estimator works on the semiparametric model <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math>, regardless of the form of the estimators, without imposing any additional restrictions, such as parametric models, SRI always has a lower semiparametric efficiency bound and the proposed estimator in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> attains this bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">From this theoretical analysis, it is expected that when the machine learning predictions already achieve high classification accuracy, there should not be much efficiency gain in reality. This is because the efficiency gains come from the fact that the machine learning predictions do not necessarily satisfy the independence constraint, but if they are almost accurate, there is no reason to expect that the residual term <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> will become large. I confirm this conjecture in the application section (Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Empirical Application ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) and the simulation section (Section <a href="#A5" title="Appendix S5 Simulation Studies ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix S2 </span>How to test assumptions in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Extension: The Proposed Methodology with Noisy Human Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> that are not guaranteed by design</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Extension: The Proposed Methodology with Noisy Human Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> has developed a methodology to account for human annotations with non-differential measurement errors, the proposed SRI approach relies on several additional assumptions. Three specific assumptions warrant particular attention: (1) the independent coding (Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption7" title="Assumption 7 (Conditional Independence of Human Annotations) ‣ 4.1 Assumptions and nonparametric identification ‣ 4 Extension: The Proposed Methodology with Noisy Human Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> (a)), which states that the coding errors are independent across coders, (2) the exclusion restriction (Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption7" title="Assumption 7 (Conditional Independence of Human Annotations) ‣ 4.1 Assumptions and nonparametric identification ‣ 4 Extension: The Proposed Methodology with Noisy Human Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> (b)), which posits that texts influence the human annotations solely through the true concept, and (3) accurate human labels (Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption8" title="Assumption 8 (Accuracy of Human Annotations) ‣ 4.1 Assumptions and nonparametric identification ‣ 4 Extension: The Proposed Methodology with Noisy Human Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> (a)), which asserts that the accuracy of the human annotated labels is more than 0.5. None of these assumptions can be directly tested or is guaranteed by the study design, thus complicating the application of the proposed methodology.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="356.54" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 568.05 356.54" width="568.05"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,356.54) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(132.4,0) translate(0,326.74)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E6E6FF;" fill="#E6E6FF"><path d="M 126.59 29.53 L -126.59 29.53 C -129.65 29.53 -132.12 27.05 -132.12 23.99 L -132.12 -23.99 C -132.12 -27.05 -129.65 -29.53 -126.59 -29.53 L 126.59 -29.53 C 129.65 -29.53 132.12 -27.05 132.12 -23.99 L 132.12 23.99 C 132.12 27.05 129.65 29.53 126.59 29.53 Z M -132.12 -29.53"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -127.51 -15.7)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 36.78)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 21.79)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 24.48)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 9.49)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 103.38 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.49em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.18" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="48.27"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.F1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1</span>:</span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 21.79)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:18.4em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="254.64"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">Create the rigid coding rule and the small</span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 34.09)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 15.53 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:16.24em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="224.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">number of the true labels by yourself</span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E6E6FF;" fill="#E6E6FF"><path d="M 107.81 -69.45 L -107.81 -69.45 C -110.87 -69.45 -113.35 -71.93 -113.35 -74.99 L -113.35 -122.97 C -113.35 -126.03 -110.87 -128.51 -107.81 -128.51 L 107.81 -128.51 C 110.87 -128.51 113.35 -126.03 113.35 -122.97 L 113.35 -74.99 C 113.35 -71.93 110.87 -69.45 107.81 -69.45 Z M -113.35 -128.51"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -108.74 -113.33)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 34.09)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 21.79)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 21.79)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 9.49)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 84.6 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.49em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.18" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="48.27"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.F1.pic1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2</span>:</span></span></fo