</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Theorem 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps"> (Asymptotic Normality with Augmented Outcome)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (True Coding Rule) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> to <a href="#Thmassumption6" title="Assumption 6 (Noisy Human Annotations) ‣ 4.1 Assumptions and nonparametric identification ‣ 4 Extension: The Proposed Methodology with Noisy Human Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption9" title="Assumption 9 (Regularity conditions for augmented-outcome SRI) ‣ Appendix S3 Extension: Use of Machine Learning Predictions ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, the estimator for the covariate-adjusted mean <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Psi}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Psi}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained by solving the estimating equation in Equation <a href="#A3.E3" title="In Appendix S3 Extension: Use of Machine Learning Predictions ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S3</span></a> for <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the asymptotic normality:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\sqrt{N}(\hat{\Psi}_{t}-\Psi_{t}^{*})}{\breve{\sigma}}\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>˘</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\sqrt{N}(\hat{\Psi}_{t}-\Psi_{t}^{*})}{\breve{\sigma}}\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\breve{\sigma}^{2}=\mathbb{E}[\nu_{t}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i},\hat{L}_{i},S_{i},\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>˘</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\breve{\sigma}^{2}=\mathbb{E}[\nu_{t}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i},\hat{L}_{i},S_{i},\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is omitted, as the result follows directly from Proposition 1 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Egami et al. (2024)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix S4 </span>Theoretical Results</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">S4.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Existence of Surrogate Representation) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">I first prove that <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ \{L_{i},T_{i}\}\mid\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ \{L_{i},T_{i}\}\mid\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Now,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})\mid\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})\mid\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})\mid\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})\mid\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})\mid\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})\mid\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">which means that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\{\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\}\mid\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\{\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\}\mid\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is a trivial example of surrogate representations.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, I prove the main statement: <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\{\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\{\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> holds if and only if <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=b(\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=b(\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math> for some function <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that there exists some function <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=b(\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=b(\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex49.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[b(\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[b(\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=b(\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=b(\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first line is by the law of iterated expectation.
Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ \bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\ \mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ \bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\ \mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">and thus <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is a surrogate representation.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the converse, suppose that <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is a surrogate representation, but <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is not finer than <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. This means that there exist <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{Y}_{j},\bm{Z}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{Y}_{j},\bm{Z}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{Y}_{k},\bm{Z}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{Y}_{k},\bm{Z}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq k</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{j},\bm{Z}_{j})=\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{k},\bm{Z}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{j},\bm{Z}_{j})=\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{k},\bm{Z}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> but <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(\bm{Y}_{j},\bm{Z}_{j})\neq\eta(\bm{Y}_{k},\bm{Z}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(\bm{Y}_{j},\bm{Z}_{j})\neq\eta(\bm{Y}_{k},\bm{Z}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. However, then</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\eta(\bm{Y}_{j},\bm{Z}_{j})=\mathbb{P}(T_{j},\tilde{L}_{j}\mid\bm{Y}_{j},\bm{Z}_{j})\neq\mathbb{P}(T_{k},\tilde{L}_{k}\mid\bm{Y}_{k},\bm{Z}_{k})=\eta(\bm{Y}_{k},\bm{Z}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta(\bm{Y}_{j},\bm{Z}_{j})=\mathbb{P}(T_{j},\tilde{L}_{j}\mid\bm{Y}_{j},\bm{Z}_{j})\neq\mathbb{P}(T_{k},\tilde{L}_{k}\mid\bm{Y}_{k},\bm{Z}_{k})=\eta(\bm{Y}_{k},\bm{Z}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{j},\bm{Z}_{j})=\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{k},\bm{Z}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{j},\bm{Z}_{j})=\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{k},\bm{Z}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, this means that within each strata of <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, the independence does not hold; i.e., <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\}\not\!\perp\!\!\!\perp\{\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><menclose notation="updiagonalstrike"><mspace style="width:-0.17em;" width="-0.17em"></mspace></menclose></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.518em;" width="0.518em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{T_{i},\tilde{L}_{i}\}\not\!\perp\!\!\!\perp\{\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. However, this contradicts with the statement that <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is a surrogate representation. Therefore, to be a surrogate representation, <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> must be finer than <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">S4.2 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Identification under Perfect Annotations) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (Identification of Target Parameter)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1 (Surrogate Representation of Texts) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;\{\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\}\mid\bm{W}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;\{\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\}\mid\bm{W}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the use of Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (True Coding Rule) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> yields</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;L_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;L_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now, notice that Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Human Annotation Sampling) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> indicates the marginal independence <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the deterministic function of <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Human Annotation Sampling) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, I can claim</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{Y}_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}\;\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{Y}_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}\;\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">because</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y},S_{i}=s\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y},S_{i}=s\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex58.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y},S_{i}=s,\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)}{\mathbb{P}(\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y},S_{i}=s,\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)}{\mathbb{P}(\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y},\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)\;\mathbb{P}(S_{i}=s)}{\mathbb{P}(\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y},\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)\;\mathbb{P}(S_{i}=s)}{\mathbb{P}(\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y}\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)\;\mathbb{P}(S_{i}=s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y}\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)\;\mathbb{P}(S_{i}=s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y}\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)\;\mathbb{P}(S_{i}=s\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y}\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)\;\mathbb{P}(S_{i}=s\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> and any pair of Borel sets <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B</annotation></semantics></math>. In the above transformation, I apply Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Human Annotation Sampling) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and the fact that <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the deterministic function of <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in the second line, and the final line is because <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. By applying Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (True Coding Rule) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, I obtain</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}\;\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}\;\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi_{t}:=\mathbb{E}\biggl[\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid T_{i}=t,\bm{Z}_{i}]\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi_{t}:=\mathbb{E}\biggl[\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid T_{i}=t,\bm{Z}_{i}]\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex62.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid T_{i}=t,\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid T_{i}=t,\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i}]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i}]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> is the support of the latent representation <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{i}=\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{i}=\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. In the transformations above, I use the law of iterated expectation in the first line, Equation <a href="#A4.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ S4.2 Proof of Proposition (Identification of Target Parameter) ‣ Appendix S4 Theoretical Results ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S4</span></a>
in the second line, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ \bm{Z}_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ \bm{Z}_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (Equation (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In Definition 1 (Surrogate Representation of Texts) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)) in the third line, Equation <a href="#A4.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ S4.2 Proof of Proposition (Identification of Target Parameter) ‣ Appendix S4 Theoretical Results ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S6</span></a> in the fourth line, and Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Perfect Annotations) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> in the last line. As <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is observed under <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> by definition, I can estimate both <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)</annotation></semantics></math> from the data.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, I show that <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}</annotation></semantics></math> does not need to be unique. Notice that the formula above is equivalent to</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi_{t}=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi_{t}=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniquely specified by researchers but <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is estimated from data and might not be unique. Suppose that there exists another <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}^{\prime}=\bm{f}^{\prime}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}^{\prime}=\bm{f}^{\prime}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{T_{i},L_{i}\}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;\{\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\}\mid\bm{W}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{T_{i},L_{i}\}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;\{\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}\}\mid\bm{W}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex68.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}^{\prime}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}^{\prime}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}^{\prime}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}^{\prime}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, I can say that the different <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}</annotation></semantics></math> still leads to the same identification formula.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">S4.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Efficient Influence Function) ‣ 3.2 Estimation and inference ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (Efficient Influence Function)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">I split the proof to the two parts.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">STEP 1: Deriving Influence function</span>: Firstly, I derive the influence function. Here, I use the technique called point-mass contamination approach <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kennedy, 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hines et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hines et al. (2022)</a></cite>, I assume that <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> are continuous only for the notational convenience, but as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hines et al. (2022)</a></cite> discussed, the entire proof works with discrete variables or a mix of discrete and continuous variables.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> be a true data distribution and <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{t}(\mathcal{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{t}(\mathcal{P})</annotation></semantics></math> be an estimand under <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=t\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=t\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and true data distribution <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. That is,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi_{t}(\mathcal{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi_{t}(\mathcal{P})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex72.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mu_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y},\bm{z}))f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mu_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y},\bm{z}))f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),S_{i}=1]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},S_{i}=1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),S_{i}=1]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},S_{i}=1]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> is the expectation operator under the distribution <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathcal{P}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathcal{P}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the PDF under the true distribution <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, consider the parametric submodel <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}=(1-\epsilon)\mathcal{P}+\epsilon\tilde{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}=(1-\epsilon)\mathcal{P}+\epsilon\tilde{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the point mass at <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{t},\tilde{\bm{y}},\tilde{l},\tilde{\bm{z}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>l</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{t},\tilde{\bm{y}},\tilde{l},\tilde{\bm{z}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the influence of perturbation in the direction of <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\Psi_{t}(\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}=\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y},\bm{z}))f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\Psi_{t}(\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}=\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y},\bm{z}))f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),S_{i}=1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}),S_{i}=1]</annotation></semantics></math> is the outcome model under <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> is the expectation operator under <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the CDF under <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math> can be regarded as a composite function, for the sake of simplicity, let <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mu_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mu_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, under the regularity condition, I can switch the derivative and integrals, and thus the chain rule yields</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\,f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\,f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\quad=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\frac{d}{d\epsilon}m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}\,f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\quad=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\frac{d}{d\epsilon}m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}\,f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad+\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}m_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\,f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad+\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}m_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\,f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad+\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}m_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\,f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{z})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}d\bm{y}d\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad+\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}m_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\,f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{z})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}d\bm{y}d\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">For the first component,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\frac{d}{d\epsilon}m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}\,f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\frac{d}{d\epsilon}m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}\,f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
