<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(1/c_{2}^{2}+1)\delta_{n}\cdot\mathbb{E}\biggl[|\mu(\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))|^{2}\biggr]^{\frac{1}{2}}+\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl|\frac{{\hat{\rho}_{t}(\hat{\bm{f}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))}}{{\hat{\pi}_{t}(\bm{Z}_{i})}}\biggr|^{2}\biggr]^{\frac{1}{2}}\cdot c_{1}\delta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(1/c_{2}^{2}+1)\delta_{n}\cdot\mathbb{E}\biggl[|\mu(\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))|^{2}\biggr]^{\frac{1}{2}}+\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl|\frac{{\hat{\rho}_{t}(\hat{\bm{f}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}))}}{{\hat{\pi}_{t}(\bm{Z}_{i})}}\biggr|^{2}\biggr]^{\frac{1}{2}}\cdot c_{1}\delta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex167"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq c_{1}(1+1/c_{2}^{2}+1/c_{2})\delta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq c_{1}(1+1/c_{2}^{2}+1/c_{2})\delta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the third line is by triangular inequality, the fourth line is by Cauchy-Schwartz inequality, and the last line is by <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[|\tilde{L}_{i}|^{2}]^{\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[|\tilde{L}_{i}|^{2}]^{\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4 (Regularity Conditions) ‣ 3.2 Estimation and inference ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A4.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{23}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>23</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{23}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
