<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex230.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\tilde{L}_{i}^{(j)}=l\mid L_{i})\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mathbb{P}(\bm{Z}_{i}=\bm{z}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},L_{i})dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid L_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\tilde{L}_{i}^{(j)}=l\mid L_{i})\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mathbb{P}(\bm{Z}_{i}=\bm{z}\mid\bm{Y}_{i},L_{i})dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid L_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex231"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex231.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\tilde{L}_{i}^{(j)}=l\mid L_{i})\mathbb{P}(\bm{Z}_{i}=\bm{z}\mid L_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\tilde{L}_{i}^{(j)}=l\mid L_{i})\mathbb{P}(\bm{Z}_{i}=\bm{z}\mid L_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second and sixth equalities are by Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (True Coding Rule) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the third equality is by Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption6" title="Assumption 6 (Noisy Human Annotations) ‣ 4.1 Assumptions and nonparametric identification ‣ 4 Extension: The Proposed Methodology with Noisy Human Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, and the fourth equality is by Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (True Coding Rule) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption7" title="Assumption 7 (Conditional Independence of Human Annotations) ‣ 4.1 Assumptions and nonparametric identification ‣ 4 Extension: The Proposed Methodology with Noisy Human Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> (<math id="A4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{i}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ \bm{Y}_{i}\mid L_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{i}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ \bm{Y}_{i}\mid L_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>).
Therefore, I have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{L}_{i}^{(j)}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ \bm{Z}_{i}\mid L_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{L}_{i}^{(j)}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ \bm{Z}_{i}\mid L_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Based on this, I have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx93" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex232"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex232.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\tilde{L}_{i}=l\mid\bm{Y}_{i},L_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mathbb{P}(\tilde{L}_{i}=l\mid\bm{Y}_{i},L_{i})=\mathbb{P}(\tilde{L}_{i}=l\mid L_{i})=\mathbb{P}(\tilde{L}_{i}=l\mid L_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\tilde{L}_{i}=l\mid\bm{Y}_{i},L_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mathbb{P}(\tilde{L}_{i}=l\mid\bm{Y}_{i},L_{i})=\mathbb{P}(\tilde{L}_{i}=l\mid L_{i})=\mathbb{P}(\tilde{L}_{i}=l\mid L_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the first equality is by Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption6" title="Assumption 6 (Noisy Human Annotations) ‣ 4.1 Assumptions and nonparametric identification ‣ 4 Extension: The Proposed Methodology with Noisy Human Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, the second is by Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption7" title="Assumption 7 (Conditional Independence of Human Annotations) ‣ 4.1 Assumptions and nonparametric identification ‣ 4 Extension: The Proposed Methodology with Noisy Human Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> (exclusion restriction), and the last equality is by Equation (<a href="#A4.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ S4.5 Proof of Proposition (Identification with Noisy Human Annotations) ‣ Appendix S4 Theoretical Results ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S10</span></a>). Thus, I have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{L}_{i}^{(j)}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ \bm{Y}_{i}\mid L_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{L}_{i}^{(j)}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ \bm{Y}_{i}\mid L_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Also,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx95" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex233"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
