<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex361.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\quad\quad\quad+|g\bigl(X_{c}^{(2)},{p}_{c}^{(2)},{q}_{c}^{(2)}\bigr)|\biggl|g\bigl(X_{c}^{(1)},\hat{p}_{c}^{(1)},\hat{q}_{c}^{(1)}\bigr)-g\bigl(X_{c}^{(1)},{p}_{c}^{(1)},{q}_{c}^{(1)}\bigr)\biggr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\quad\quad\quad+|g\bigl(X_{c}^{(2)},{p}_{c}^{(2)},{q}_{c}^{(2)}\bigr)|\biggl|g\bigl(X_{c}^{(1)},\hat{p}_{c}^{(1)},\hat{q}_{c}^{(1)}\bigr)-g\bigl(X_{c}^{(1)},{p}_{c}^{(1)},{q}_{c}^{(1)}\bigr)\biggr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex362"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex362.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{c_{3}}\biggl(\biggl|g\bigl(X_{c}^{(2)},\hat{p}_{c}^{(2)},\hat{q}_{c}^{(2)}\bigr)-g\bigl(X_{c}^{(2)},{p}_{c}^{(2)},{q}_{c}^{(2)}\bigr)\biggr|+\biggl|g\bigl(X_{c}^{(1)},\hat{p}_{c}^{(1)},\hat{q}_{c}^{(1)}\bigr)-g\bigl(X_{c}^{(1)},{p}_{c}^{(1)},{q}_{c}^{(1)}\bigr)\biggr|\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{c_{3}}\biggl(\biggl|g\bigl(X_{c}^{(2)},\hat{p}_{c}^{(2)},\hat{q}_{c}^{(2)}\bigr)-g\bigl(X_{c}^{(2)},{p}_{c}^{(2)},{q}_{c}^{(2)}\bigr)\biggr|+\biggl|g\bigl(X_{c}^{(1)},\hat{p}_{c}^{(1)},\hat{q}_{c}^{(1)}\bigr)-g\bigl(X_{c}^{(1)},{p}_{c}^{(1)},{q}_{c}^{(1)}\bigr)\biggr|\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex363"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex363.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{c_{3}^{3}}\biggl(|\hat{p}_{c}^{(1)}-{p}_{c}^{(1)}|+|\hat{q}_{c}^{(1)}-{q}_{c}^{(1)}|+|\hat{p}_{c}^{(2)}-{p}_{c}^{(2)}|+|\hat{q}_{c}^{(2)}-{q}_{c}^{(2)}|\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{c_{3}^{3}}\biggl(|\hat{p}_{c}^{(1)}-{p}_{c}^{(1)}|+|\hat{q}_{c}^{(1)}-{q}_{c}^{(1)}|+|\hat{p}_{c}^{(2)}-{p}_{c}^{(2)}|+|\hat{q}_{c}^{(2)}-{q}_{c}^{(2)}|\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS8.p3.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS8.p3.13.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality is by triangular inequality, the second is by Cauchy-Schwartz inequality, the third is by Equation (<a href="#A4.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ S4.8 Proof of Theorem (Asymptotic Normality) ‣ Appendix S4 Theoretical Results ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S16</span></a>), and the last is by Equation (<a href="#A4.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ S4.8 Proof of Theorem (Asymptotic Normality) ‣ Appendix S4 Theoretical Results ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S15</span></a>). Now, by Cauchy-Schwartz,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx143" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex364"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex364.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle(a_{1}+a_{2}+a_{3}+a_{4})^{2}=\biggl(\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}a_{1}&amp;a_{2}&amp;a_{3}&amp;a_{4}\end{bmatrix}^{\scriptscriptstyle\mathsf{T}}}_{:=\bm{a}}\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;1&amp;1&amp;1\end{bmatrix}}_{:=\mathbf{1}^{\scriptscriptstyle\mathsf{T}}}\biggr)^{2}\leq\lVert\bm{a}\rVert^{2}\lVert\mathbf{1}\rVert^{2}=4(a_{1}^{2}+a_{2}^{2}+a_{3}^{2}+a_{4}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>𝖳</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(a_{1}+a_{2}+a_{3}+a_{4})^{2}=\biggl(\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}a_{1}&amp;a_{2}&amp;a_{3}&amp;a_{4}\end{bmatrix}^{\scriptscriptstyle\mathsf{T}}}_{:=\bm{a}}\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;1&amp;1&amp;1\end{bmatrix}}_{:=\mathbf{1}^{\scriptscriptstyle\mathsf{T}}}\biggr)^{2}\leq\lVert\bm{a}\rVert^{2}\lVert\mathbf{1}\rVert^{2}=4(a_{1}^{2}+a_{2}^{2}+a_{3}^{2}+a_{4}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS8.p3.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS8.p3.14.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="A4.SS8.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying this, I obtain</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx144" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex365"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex365.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\biggl|\hat{M}_{c}(\tilde{L}_{i}^{(1)},\tilde{L}_{i}^{(2)})-M_{c}(\tilde{L}_{i}^{(1)},\tilde{L}_{i}^{(2)})\biggr|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\biggl|\hat{M}_{c}(\tilde{L}_{i}^{(1)},\tilde{L}_{i}^{(2)})-M_{c}(\tilde{L}_{i}^{(1)},\tilde{L}_{i}^{(2)})\biggr|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex365.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{4}{c_{3}^{6}}\biggl(|\hat{p}_{c}^{(1)}-{p}_{c}^{(1)}|^{2}+|\hat{q}_{c}^{(1)}-{q}_{c}^{(1)}|^{2}+|\hat{p}_{c}^{(2)}-{p}_{c}^{(2)}|^{2}+|\hat{q}_{c}^{(2)}-{q}_{c}^{(2)}|^{2}\biggr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn><mn>6</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{4}{c_{3}^{6}}\biggl(|\hat{p}_{c}^{(1)}-{p}_{c}^{(1)}|^{2}+|\hat{q}_{c}^{(1)}-{q}_{c}^{(1)}|^{2}+|\hat{p}_{c}^{(2)}-{p}_{c}^{(2)}|^{2}+|\hat{q}_{c}^{(2)}-{q}_{c}^{(2)}|^{2}\biggr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS8.p3.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS8.p3.15.1" class="ltx_text">By taking the expectation, I finally get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx145" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex366"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex366.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl|\hat{M}_{c}(\tilde{L}_{i}^{(1)},\tilde{L}_{i}^{(2)})-M_{c}(\tilde{L}_{i}^{(1)},\tilde{L}_{i}^{(2)})\biggr|^{2}\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl|\hat{M}_{c}(\tilde{L}_{i}^{(1)},\tilde{L}_{i}^{(2)})-M_{c}(\tilde{L}_{i}^{(1)},\tilde{L}_{i}^{(2)})\biggr|^{2}\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex367"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex367.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{4}{c_{3}^{6}}\biggl\{\mathbb{E}\biggl[|\hat{p}_{c}^{(1)}-{p}_{c}^{(1)}|^{2}\biggr]+\mathbb{E}\biggl[|\hat{q}_{c}^{(1)}-{q}_{c}^{(1)}|^{2}\biggr]+\mathbb{E}\biggl[|\hat{p}_{c}^{(2)}-{p}_{c}^{(2)}|^{2}\biggr]+\mathbb{E}\biggl[|\hat{q}_{c}^{(2)}-{q}_{c}^{(2)}|^{2}\biggr]\biggr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn><mn>6</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{4}{c_{3}^{6}}\biggl\{\mathbb{E}\biggl[|\hat{p}_{c}^{(1)}-{p}_{c}^{(1)}|^{2}\biggr]+\mathbb{E}\biggl[|\hat{q}_{c}^{(1)}-{q}_{c}^{(1)}|^{2}\biggr]+\mathbb{E}\biggl[|\hat{p}_{c}^{(2)}-{p}_{c}^{(2)}|^{2}\biggr]+\mathbb{E}\biggl[|\hat{q}_{c}^{(2)}-{q}_{c}^{(2)}|^{2}\biggr]\biggr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex368"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex368.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{4}{c_{3}^{6}}\biggl(o_{p}(n^{-1/2})+o_{p}(n^{-1/2})+o_{p}(n^{-1/2})+o_{p}(n^{-1/2})\biggr)=o_{p}(n^{-1/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn><mn>6</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{4}{c_{3}^{6}}\biggl(o_{p}(n^{-1/2})+o_{p}(n^{-1/2})+o_{p}(n^{-1/2})+o_{p}(n^{-1/2})\biggr)=o_{p}(n^{-1/2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS8.p3.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS8.p3.16.1" class="ltx_text">where the last line is by using Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption10" title="Assumption 10 (Regularity Conditions) ‣ S4.8 Proof of Theorem (Asymptotic Normality) ‣ Appendix S4 Theoretical Results ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. Hence, combined with the first inequality I derived, I prove that the outcome model with the estimated surrogate outcomes achieves <math id="A4.SS8.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> convergence under all the stated conditions at the convergence rate <math id="A4.SS8.p3.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="n^{-1/4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{-1/4}</annotation></semantics></math>, which in the end implies the rate double robustness I have in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4 (Regularity Conditions) ‣ 3.2 Estimation and inference ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. The exact same proof applies to the part that the <math id="A4.SS8.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm is bounded by the constant <math id="A4.SS8.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. As the efficient influence function takes mathematically equivalent expressions, the rest of the proof follows directly from Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Asymptotic Normality) ‣ 3.2 Estimation and inference ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix S5 </span>Simulation Studies</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">S5.1 </span>Case 1: Perfect Human Annotations</h3>

<section id="A5.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">S5.1.1 </span>Simulation setup</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">I conduct simulation studies to evaluate the empirical performance of the proposed SRI estimator and to compare it with existing estimators. Because it is extremely difficult to generate realistic text data that are systematically influenced by predictors in a synthetic experiment, I instead generate high-dimensional vectors with dimensions comparable to standard sentence embeddings and allow them to depend on predictors through the data-generating process. Specifically, I generate data for <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=20,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20,000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=20,000</annotation></semantics></math> units according to the following process:</p>
<table id="A5.E17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A5.E17X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{i}\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(0.5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bernoulli</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{i}\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(0.5)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(S17)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.E17Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{For }j\in[1,\cdots,768]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>For </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>768</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{For }j\in[1,\cdots,768]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.E17Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E17Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{1j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}[0.0,1.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{1j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}[0.0,1.0]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.E17Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E17Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{ij}=\alpha_{1j}T_{i}+\epsilon_{ij},\quad\epsilon_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{ij}=\alpha_{1j}T_{i}+\epsilon_{ij},\quad\epsilon_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.E17Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E17Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{L}_{i}=\mathbbm{1}\{\sigma(1.0+0.2\cdot\mathbf{1}^{\intercal}\bm{Y}_{i})&gt;0.5\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊺</mo></msup><mi>𝒀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{L}_{i}=\mathbbm{1}\{\sigma(1.0+0.2\cdot\mathbf{1}^{\intercal}\bm{Y}_{i})&gt;0.5\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">I then artificially generate machine-predicted labels <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with accuracies ranging from 70% to 90% by randomly flipping the value of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> according to the selected error percentage (e.g., when the accuracy of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> s set to 90%, 10% of the values of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are randomly changed).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To implement the proposed SRI estimator, I use 2-fold cross-fitting with the neural network architecture illustrated in Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.2 Estimation and inference ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. The network consists of three shared layers with dimensions 100, 100, and 50, producing the shared representation <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}(\bm{R}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}(\bm{R}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. This shared layer is then connected to two prediction heads—one for the outcome and one for the predictor of interest—each composed of two layers with dimensions 50 and 1, respectively. I use ReLU activations and solve the optimization problem in Equation <a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.2 Estimation and inference ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math> using the Adam optimizer, a learning rate of 0.00002, a maximum of 200 epochs, and a batch size of 256 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma and Ba, 2017</a>)</cite>. I reserve 20% of the data for validation and apply early stopping with a patience of five epochs to prevent overfitting (i.e., training stops if the validation loss does not decrease for five consecutive epochs). Once the outcome model and surrogacy score are estimated, I compute the difference in outcome means using the estimating equation in Equation (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In item 3 ‣ 3.2 Estimation and inference ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As in the empirical application in Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Empirical Application ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, I evaluate the performance of the proposed estimator by comparing it with existing bias-correction methods, Prediction-Powered Inference (PPI, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Angelopoulos et al. 2023</a></cite> and Design-Based Supervised Learning (DSL; <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Egami et al. 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Egami et al. 2024</a></cite>). For simplicity, I omit control variables <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> from this simulation. When <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is included, the proposed estimator must additionally estimate the propensity score, which may introduce efficiency differences relative to alternative methods that do not require this step <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hirano et al., 2003</a>)</cite>. Given the simplicity of the data-generating process, this simulation design allows me to clearly assess the extent to which the imposed independence constraint improves efficiency.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">S5.1.2 </span>Simulation results</h4>

<figure id="A5.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.12416v2/sim_perfect.svg" id="A5.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:626/222;" width="626" height="222"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure S2</span>: </span><span id="A5.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance comparison between the Surrogate Representation Inference (SRI, proposed) and the existing bias-correction algorithms that corrects measurement error from machine learning predictions (PPI; <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Angelopoulos et al. 2023</a></cite> and DSL; <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Egami et al. 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Egami et al. 2024</a></cite>). I use the human annotations with no mistakes, and vary the classification accuracy of machine learning predictions (from 0.70 to 0.90). All results are based on 200 Monte Carlo simulations.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A5.F2" title="Figure S2 ‣ S5.1.2 Simulation results ‣ S5.1 Case 1: Perfect Human Annotations ‣ Appendix S5 Simulation Studies ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S2</span></a> presents the results of the simulation studies with perfectly observed human-annotated labels based on 200 Monte Carlo replications. Numerical results are reported in Table <a href="#A5.T1" title="Table S1 ‣ S5.1.2 Simulation results ‣ S5.1 Case 1: Perfect Human Annotations ‣ Appendix S5 Simulation Studies ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The results show that the proposed SRI method outperforms existing bias-correction techniques across all levels of classification accuracy for the proxy labels <math id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Although existing bias-correction approaches correct for prediction errors, they suffer from large root mean squared errors (RMSEs) and large standard errors, particularly when classification accuracy ranges from 70% to 80%. As a consequence, their estimated standard errors are also inflated. For example, at 80% classification accuracy, the average standard error for the existing approach is 0.020, compared to 0.014 for the proposed SRI estimator. This difference indicates that even at moderately high classification accuracy levels, such as 80%, the proposed estimator achieves a substantial reduction in estimation uncertainty.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Overall, these results confirm that the SRI estimator provides a useful alternative to existing bias-correction techniques, especially in settings where researchers only have access to machine-learning predictions with moderate classification accuracy.</p>
</div>
